{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And a woman shall ask.</b> As an outright gift, as in 'ask of me and I shall give,' etc. — for I shall grant this people favor in the eyes of the Egyptians." "<b>And a woman shall ask.</b> The men too asked, but the verse speaks of the customary practice, since women are accustomed to ask for jewelry more than men. And likewise the verse mentioned a female sorcerer, because of the customary practice." "<b>Vessels of silver and vessels of gold and garments.</b> For the honor of the festival that you shall celebrate for Me in the wilderness." "<b>And you shall despoil the Egyptians.</b> As wages for the bondage of forced labor."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:56:02.214686339Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}